## On the job {.unnumbered}

::: callout-important
## Why this matters day to day

Attrition, promotion, time-to-productivity for new hires, time until a
first internal move — almost every "how long until X" question in the
employee lifecycle is a survival question, and almost all of that data
is censored (anyone still in the state you're measuring is a censored
observation, not a clean zero). Reaching for a plain classifier on this
kind of data is one of the most common avoidable mistakes in People
Analytics — it silently discards timing information and mishandles
everyone still "in progress."
:::

